<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Flores Race Planner (pipeline/export_gpx.py)" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1 http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1/gpx.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <name>S10 Egon and the far east</name>
    <desc>Section 10 of the Flores Race traverse: The crux logistics question of the whole race. 190.9 km, +3776 m / -3785 m, starts at km 1141 of the course.</desc>
    <link href="https://github.com/technicaloutdoor/Flores-Race"><text>Flores Race Planner</text></link>
    <time>2026-09-05T06:27:58Z</time>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="-8.624377" lon="122.210411">
    <ele>24.8</ele>
    <name>Maumere</name>
    <desc>km 0.0 | kind: town | resupply: full | water: reliable | sleep: hotel -- Capital of Sikka Regency and the largest town of the eastern half of the island: market, ATMs, hospital (RSUD dr. TC Hillers), bike-ish parts, hotels. Frans Seda Airport is 5 km out (see p-frans-seda-airport). Rebuilt af</desc>
    <sym>City (Medium)</sym>
    <type>anchor/town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.698000" lon="122.313000">
    <ele>452.8</ele>
    <name>Watublapi</name>
    <desc>km 29.4 | kind: village | resupply: minimal | water: unreliable | sleep: homestay | position approximate -- Hillside ikat-weaving hamlet (Dusun Watublapi, Desa Kajowair, Kecamatan Hewokloang), about 18 km / 30 min inland-south-east of Maumere. No source gives coordinates for the hamlet itself; placed at the Hewokloang kecamata</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.662230" lon="122.447690">
    <ele>786.2</ele>
    <name>Blidit</name>
    <desc>km 70.9 | kind: trailhead | resupply: none | water: unreliable | sleep: none | position approximate -- Last village before the Egon volcano trail, reached from Waigete (about 19 km east of Maumere on the highway) via an 8-9 km side road. A trip report gives the trailhead elevation as 788 m; this point was found by samplin</desc>
    <sym>Trail Head</sym>
    <type>anchor/trailhead</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.606500" lon="122.475000">
    <ele>10.8</ele>
    <name>Waiterang</name>
    <desc>km 85.7 | kind: village | resupply: minimal | water: unreliable | sleep: guesthouse -- North-coast dive village east of Maumere (Waigete kecamatan), on the same stretch as the Wodong dive sites; a small dive resort operates here. No dedicated source pins Waiterang itself; position taken from two closely ag</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.545100" lon="122.517400">
    <ele>3.6</ele>
    <name>Talibura</name>
    <desc>km 95.4 | kind: village | resupply: basic | water: unreliable | sleep: none | position approximate -- Easternmost and largest kecamatan of Sikka Regency, on the Flores Sea coast approaching the Flores Timur border; has a mangrove coast (Desa Darat Pantai). Two Wikidata entries for 'Talibura' disagree by several km and bo</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.347500" lon="122.979700">
    <ele>13.0</ele>
    <name>Larantuka</name>
    <desc>km 190.9 | kind: finish | resupply: full | water: reliable | sleep: hotel -- Race finish town: capital of Flores Timur Regency, historic Portuguese-Catholic port under Ile Mandiri, host of the Semana Santa Holy Week procession. Also a port (ferries to Adonara, Solor, Lembata, Kupang) and near Gew</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Red</sym>
    <type>anchor/finish</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.746350" lon="122.296860">
    <ele>0.9</ele>
    <name>Bola South Coast</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position unverified] South-coast stretch around Bola village, anchor of the optional Ultra-variant loop (Maumere -&gt; Bola -&gt; Watublapi -&gt; Egon); quieter and less documented than the Paga/Koka coast further west.</desc>
    <sym>Beach</sym>
    <type>poi/beach</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.676200" lon="122.455600">
    <ele>1666.1</ele>
    <name>Mount Egon</name>
    <desc>[highlight, hike-a-bike] Active stratovolcano east of Maumere; summit commonly cited at 1,661-1,703 m (sources disagree) with a crater lake and fumaroles, climbed from Blidit village. Frequent phreatic activity since reawakening in 2004.</desc>
    <sym>Summit</sym>
    <type>poi/volcano</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.314800" lon="122.968000">
    <ele>1469.4</ele>
    <name>Ile Mandiri</name>
    <desc>[highlight, hike-a-bike] Dormant volcano (commonly cited 1,502 m, DEM peak ~1,469 m) rising directly behind Larantuka; the mountain the finish town sits under, and the subject of a proposed optional final hike-a-bike 'sting in the tail'.</desc>
    <sym>Summit</sym>
    <type>poi/volcano</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.346500" lon="122.980000">
    <ele>21.6</ele>
    <name>Kapela Tuan Ma</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position unverified] Small waterfront chapel housing the venerated Tuan Ma (Our Lady) statue, the focal point of Larantuka's Semana Santa: on Good Friday the statue is carried in procession to Kapela Tuan Ana and back through the town.</desc>
    <sym>Church</sym>
    <type>poi/religious</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.347000" lon="122.979700">
    <ele>16.4</ele>
    <name>Reinha Rosari Cathedral</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position unverified] Seat of the Roman Catholic Diocese of Larantuka, dedicated to Mary Queen of the Rosary; the cathedral around which the Semana Santa Holy Week processions are organised each year.</desc>
    <sym>Church</sym>
    <type>poi/religious</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.347500" lon="122.979700">
    <ele>13.0</ele>
    <name>Larantuka -- Semana Santa and Portuguese Heritage</name>
    <desc>[highlight] Portuguese-Catholic port town at Flores' eastern tip, seat of the historic Kingdom of Larantuka and host of Semana Santa, a Holy Week procession tradition local sources describe as unbroken since the 16th century; the race's Portuguese-heritage bookend to Sikka in the west.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/heritage</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.665969" lon="122.187054">
    <ele>214.9</ele>
    <name>Ledalero Seminary</name>
    <desc>[highlight] St Paul's Major Seminary, founded 1937 by the Divine Word Missionaries (SVD) on a hilltop ~9 km inland from Maumere; one of the largest Catholic seminaries in the world and a marker of how deeply Catholic this end of Flores is.</desc>
    <sym>Church</sym>
    <type>poi/religious</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.606500" lon="122.475000">
    <ele>10.8</ele>
    <name>Waiterang / Wodong Coast</name>
    <desc>[highlight] North-coast dive stretch east of Maumere (Waigete kecamatan); black-sand beaches, house-reef diving and a small resort scene, on the corridor toward Egon and the far east.</desc>
    <sym>Beach</sym>
    <type>poi/beach</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.698000" lon="122.313000">
    <ele>452.8</ele>
    <name>Watublapi Ikat Weaving</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position approximate] Hillside hamlet about 18 km south-east of Maumere where Sikkanese ikat weavers still spin, naturally dye and hand-weave cotton cloth on backstrap looms, with demonstrations and cloth for sale.</desc>
    <sym>Shopping Center</sym>
    <type>poi/weaving</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.599703" lon="122.202836">
    <ele>7.2</ele>
    <name>Wuring</name>
    <desc>[highlight] Bajo (sea nomad) stilt village built out over the tidal flats at the edge of Maumere bay, a few km west of the town centre; one of Flores' few remaining Bajo settlements, passed on the way into Maumere.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/traditional-village</type>
  </wpt>
